<title>UK: Caradon gains on Weru unit results.</title>
<headline>Caradon gains on Weru unit results.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-10-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in British building materials group Caradon pushed higher in pre-market trade on Wednesday after its majority-owned German subsidiary Weru AG said it expected to meet its earnings forecasts for this year.</p>
<p>Caradon led early volumes, gaining three pence to 262-1/2p in a falling market. Some 480,000 shares had changed hands.</p>
<p>In a statement Caradon said Weru was on course to meet its forecast of a doubling results from ordinary trading activities this year. It said Weru operating profits in the first nine months were on target at 21.7 million marks.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
